			<div class="content" id="post-content-2739426">
									

<p>Extremely belated response, since I had no meaningful response in mind initially&#8230; until now (obviously).</p>
<p>When I read through SCP-1000 recently, I noted this particular line:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Supposedly a trickster forest god showed humanity favor</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And I thought: &quot;Would SCP-2511-A be that trickster forest god&quot;?</p>
<p>I mean, kappas traditionally fit the two ideas on &quot;trickster&quot; and &quot;god&quot;. The &quot;forest&quot; aspect is a bit of a stretch, unless the river is within a forest.</p>
<p>Nevertheless, the choice to use SCP-1000 for this particular crosslink is to debunk the supposed gravitas of the ancient Bigfoot-humanity conflict AND to serve as a lead-in to the punchline of this article.</p>

